  "hindi": "हम शर के पिता, सौ शक्तियों वाले पर्जन्य को जानते हैं; उसी से मैं तुम्हारे शरीर के लिए कल्याण करता हूँ; पृथ्वी पर तुम्हारा उँडेला जाना हो, तुम्हारे लिए वह बाहर हो — बाल्!",
  "english": "We know the father of the reed, Parjanya, of a hundred powers; by that I make well-being for your body: on the earth be your pouring out; let it be outside for you — bāl!",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "tanve3śaṃ: tanve with the pluta mark 3, then śam. bāl is a sound-word followed by iti. niṣecanam is read as 'pouring out'. The refrain has the same wording in units 1 to 5.",
